      "narrative": "As I reflect on my time in the cramped galley, I remember the initial state of disarray, with salt having seeped into every nook and cranny. My first task was to investigate the available items, starting with the kettle, which sat dented on the floor. Upon examining it, I noticed the kettle was made of tin, and it was clear that the galley had seen its fair share of wear and tear.\n\nAfter that, I decided to leave the galley behind and head north, where I found myself in a more spacious room called the Store. The smell of paraffin lingered in the air, and I took in the largely empty shelves, which made me wonder about the purpose of this room. Among the sparse belongings, I spotted a coil of rope on the floor, which I decided to take with me for future use.",
